    "description": "SolarBank Joint Venture (New HoldCo) is a newly formed vehicle created to own and finance a portfolio of U.S. solar assets associated with SolarBank. The underlying projects serve renewable-power end markets, including community-solar and distributed-generation applications, through long-lived operating assets rather than an asset-light development advisory model. Public transaction materials describe a portfolio of 97 MW of identified U.S. renewable-energy assets to be funded through the structure. The model is asset-heavy and project-based because the vehicle is designed to acquire project interests and support construction and ownership of operating renewable infrastructure. SolarBank announced in May 2025 that CIM would provide up to $100 million of project-based financing and preferred equity through the newly formed joint-venture structure, while the ownership percentages were not publicly disclosed.",
